English

1. Scope
This notice covers only original code, skill instructions and documentation to the extent that the rights holder lawfully holds the relevant rights. Third-party software, trademarks, documentation, models and customer materials retain their own ownership and license terms.

2. Public visibility and platform rights
The source is publicly visible, but the project is not offered under an open-source license or a default free-use or trial license. This notice does not restrict rights granted by applicable law, rights granted through GitHub's Terms of Service for use of the platform, including viewing and forking, or valid permissions already granted by the rights holder. Public visibility or the ability to fork does not itself grant additional use or commercial rights beyond those sources.

3. Separate written authorization
To the extent not otherwise permitted by applicable law, platform terms or an existing valid agreement, running, modifying, integrating, deploying, redistributing, sublicensing or providing services based on the original project contents requires prior written authorization from the rights holder. Permitted purposes, deliverables, modification and distribution rights, fees and support are governed by a separate written agreement. These authorization requirements do not restrict the rights holder's own maintenance and use of the project.

4. Sponsorship and cooperation
Only sponsorship, commercial cooperation and licensing inquiries are accepted. Sponsorship alone does not grant use, commercial integration or redistribution rights unless a written agreement states otherwise.

5. Third-party rights
This project grants no license to Altium Designer, PSIM, component libraries, vendor runtimes or other third-party materials. Product and vendor names identify compatibility targets and sources only; no official affiliation, certification, sponsorship or endorsement is implied. The public repository excludes customer projects, customer screenshots, commercial libraries and copies of vendor manuals. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

6. Engineering validation and responsibility
Models, layouts and simulation results require review for the actual components, software version and intended use. Example validation is not a guarantee for all topologies, software versions, hardware performance or manufacturing safety. Applicable law and a separate written agreement determine service scope, quality requirements and responsibility. Nothing here excludes rights or liabilities that cannot lawfully be excluded.

Any interpretation differences between the Chinese and English text are resolved according to the parties' valid written agreement and applicable law.
